This makes your example render as one `markdown` block while preserving the inner `bash` fences as literal README content.

One caveat: identical nested triple-backtick fences are technically ambiguous Markdown. If you control generation, the most Markdown-compatible output is still to wrap the outer block with four backticks. But the parser change above makes the UI tolerant of the current format.

